<misterromdescription>
    <!--
        The ROM recipe.  tools/mra_build.py reads this and your MAME `bbcb`
        romset and writes bbcmicro.rom; any standard MRA tool does the same.

        The image is laid out so that each region is byte-identical to the
        region MAME loads (tools/verify_rom.py proves it):

          0x00000  64K  sideways ROM sockets, 16K each, same as MAME's "rom"
                        region, of which a Model B decodes the first four:
                          socket 0  DNFS 1.20, the disc filing system
                          socket 1  empty, FF
                          socket 2  empty, FF
                          socket 3  BASIC II, the language
          0x10000  16K  MOS 1.20, same as MAME's "mos" region
          0x14000   1K  SAA5050 character ROM, 960 bytes padded with FF,
                        same as MAME's "saa5050:chargen" from 0x140 up

        Total 0x14400 = 82,944 bytes, all of which lives in block RAM in the
        core; the disc image is a separate data slot and never appears here.
        The layout must match target/pocket/bbcmicro_mem.sv, rtl/bbc_rom.sv
        and sim/tb_mem.cpp.  docs/core-design.md section 3.

        Two notes on names and dumps, because romsets vary:

        * Merged sets often carry DNFS 1.20 as "dnfs120-201666.rom" rather
          than MAME's "dnfs120.rom".  The builder falls back to finding a
          part by CRC when the name is absent, so either works.
        * MAME's verified SAA5050 dump is CRC 201490f3 ("from datasheet
          listing and decap").  Many sets carry 6298fc0b instead, which is a
          plausible teletext font and is what MAME will use if that is what
          you have, so the core and MAME agree either way; but only 201490f3
          is the font a real SAA5050 has.  Both are accepted here, and
          verify_rom.py says which one you built with.
    -->
    <name>BBC Micro Model B</name>
    <setname>bbcmicro</setname>
    <rbf>bbcmicro</rbf>
    <mameversion>0288</mameversion>
    <year>1981</year>
    <manufacturer>Acorn Computers</manufacturer>
    <rom index="0" zip="bbcb.zip" md5="250c35fe94b9fcce90e48bd584961743">
        <!-- sideways socket 0: Acorn DNFS 1.20 (DFS 1.20 plus NFS 3.34) -->
        <part name="dnfs120.rom" crc="8ccd2157"/>
        <!-- sockets 1 and 2: empty, and an empty socket reads FF -->
        <part repeat="32768">FF</part>
        <!-- sideways socket 3: BASIC II -->
        <part name="basic2.rom" crc="79434781"/>
        <!-- the OS -->
        <part name="os12.rom" crc="3c14fc70"/>
        <!-- SAA5050 teletext character generator, 96 characters of 10 rows -->
        <part name="saa5050" crc="201490f3|6298fc0b"/>
        <part repeat="64">FF</part>
    </rom>
</misterromdescription>
